# draco-agent-hooks.skill - Phase 10: Universal Agent Integration & Hook Ecosystem

## Purpose
Phase 10 skill for universal agent integration and hook ecosystem. Works with 50+ AI coding agents through seamless integration hooks, per-agent optimization profiles, and YAGNI-first decision ladder enforcement.

## Agent Hook Development (Phase 10 Component 1)

### Hook Integration Patterns (10+ Established Patterns)

#### Pattern 1: Drop-in Replacement
```
Description: DraCo replaces existing agent optimization automatically
Configuration:
  - replacement_mode: "drop-in"
  - no_code_changes: true
  - automatic_detection: true
  - fallback_enabled: true

Use case: Claude Code users get DraCo optimization without changing workflow
```

#### Pattern 2: Parallel Operation
```
Description: DraCo runs alongside existing agent optimization
Configuration:
  - parallel_mode: true
  - separate_pipelines: true
  - unified_metrics: true
  - conflict_resolution: "auto"

Use case: DraCo optimizes while agent's native optimization continues
```

#### Pattern 3: Gradual Adoption
```
Description: DraCo introduces optimization incrementally
Configuration:
  - adoption_phases: ["phase_1", "phase_2", ...]
  - enable_per_phase: true
  - metrics_comparison: per_phase
  - rollback_on_failure: true

Use case: Team adopts DraCo one phase at a time over weeks
```

#### Pattern 4: Agent-Specific Adapter
```
Description: Custom adapter for particular agent's API/workflow
Configuration:
  - adapter_name: "claude_code", "cursor", "copilot", etc.
  - api_integration: agent's specific API endpoints
  - hook_points: where DraCo interrupts workflow
  - output_format: agent's expected output format

Use case: Full DraCo integration with unique agent APIs
```

#### Pattern 5: YAGNI Decision Ladder Enforcement
```
Description: YAGNI-first decision ladder enforced across all integrations
Configuration:
  - yonagi_ladder_level: 3 (L1-L6, L3 default)
  - auto_approve_threshold: "L3 items with >50% usage history"
  - developer_override: "// draco:keep" comment format
  - ladder_enforcement: "phases 1-6 mandatory"

Use case: Consistent YAGNI enforcement across all agents
```

#### Pattern 6: Real-Time Feedback Loop
```
Description: Real-time optimization feedback during agent workflow
Configuration:
  - real_time_updates: true
  - latency_target_ms: 100
  - quality_monitoring: continuous
  - auto_suggestions: true

Use case: DraCo suggests optimizations as agent works
```

#### Pattern 7: A/B Testing Profiles
```
Description: Continuous A/B testing of optimization profiles
Configuration:
  - ab_testing: true
  - profile_a: "current_profile"
  - profile_b: "optimized_profile"
  - improvement_threshold: 0.1% (0.1% reduction improvement)
  - auto_update: "24h" (auto-update if improvement detected)

Use case: Continuous profile improvement without developer intervention
```

#### Pattern 8: Version Compatibility Management
```
Description: Manage compatibility across agent version updates
Configuration:
  - compatibility_matrix: 50x50 agent version table
  - backward_compatible: true (to v1.0)
  - forward_compatible: true (newer agent versions)
  - deprecation_policy: "6-month notice"

Use case: DraCo works across agent major/minor version changes
```

#### Pattern 9: Multi-Agent Simultaneous Operation
```
Description: DraCo optimizes workflows with multiple agents active
Configuration:
  - multi_agent: true
  - agent_priority: ["claude_code", "cursor", ...]
  - shared_reduction: 78% (cumulative across agents)
  - quality_concerns: "minimal" (proper conflict resolution)

Use case: Office using multiple AI agents concurrently
```

#### Pattern 10: Seamless Integration Without Disruption
```
Description: DraCo integrates without interrupting existing workflows
Configuration:
  - disruption_free: true
  - zero_downtime_deployment: true
  - config_preservation: true (500+ settings)
  - rollback_on_issues: instant (to previous version)

Use case: Production systems cannot tolerate downtime
```

### Hook Development API
```
Function: generate_agent_hook()
Inputs:
  - agent_type: detected agent (claude_code, cursor, etc.)
  - phase: which of 12 phases hook applies to
  - hook_type: "pre_process" or "post_process"
  - custom_rules: optional custom YAML filter rules
  - override_ladder: override YAGNI decision (boolean)
Outputs:
  - hook_id: unique identifier for this hook configuration
  - yaml_config: YAML filter configuration for this phase
  - ml_models_to_load: which ML models to load for this agent/phase
  skill_enforcer: YAGNI decision ladder enforcement settings
  mcp_routing: MCP routing configuration for this agent/phase
  estimated_reduction: estimated token reduction from this hook
  estimated_quality: estimated quality preservation (%)
```

## Per-Agent Optimization Profiles (Phase 10 Component 2)

### 100+ Agent Profiles Summary

| Agent | Profile Name | Optimization Level | YAGNI Level | Key Features |
|-------|-------------|-------------------|-------------|-------------|
| Claude Code | claude_code_v3 | maximum | L3 (strict) | YAGNI-first, skill enforcement, 95%+ quality |
| Cursor | cursor_optimized | high | L4 (flexible) | Context-aware, real-time feedback |
| Copilot | copilot_balanced | high | L5 (with consent) | Suggestion mode, quality-focused |
| Codex | codex_comprehensive | high | L3-auto/L5-model | Multi-language, 30+ languages |
| Trae.ai | trae_optimized | medium | L4 | Cross-platform, unified profile |
| Windsurf | windsurf_medium | medium | L4 | Modern editor, incremental |
| Novita | novita_light | light | L5 | Emerging agent, few-shot |
| Generic | generic_adapter | variable | L5 (few-shot) | 50+ agents, fallback |

### Profile Configuration Example
```yaml
agent: "claude_code"
profile: "claude_code_v3"
version: "3.0"
optimization_level: "maximum"
yonagi_ladder_level: 3

compression:
  target_reduction: 95
  quality_threshold: 92
  enable_yonagi_ladder: true

phases:
  1: {enabled: true, priority: 1}
  2: {enabled: true, priority: 1}
  3: {enabled: true, priority: 2}
  4: {enabled: true, priority: 2}
  5: {enabled: true, priority: 3}
  6: {enabled: true, priority: 3}
  7: {enabled: true, priority: 4}
  8: {enabled: true, priority: 4}
  9: {enabled: true, priority: 5}
  10: {enabled: true, priority: 5}
  11: {enabled: true, priority: 6}
  12: {enabled: true, priority: 6}

filters:
  exclude_patterns:
    - "^#.*generated.*:"
    - "^##.*TODO.*$"
    - "^export.*from.*@"
  include_patterns:
    - "^function [a-z_]"
    - "^class [A-Z]"
    - "^import [a-z]"

ml_models:
  intent_classifier: "bert_base"
  importance_scorer: "sentence_transformer"
  quality_classifier: "bert_quality"
  summarizer: "pegasus_code"

continuous_learning:
  enabled: true
  auto_update: true
  feedback_frequency: "24h"
  improvement_target: 0.5
```

### Profile Auto-Detection and Selection
```
Function: detect_and_select_profile()
Inputs:
  - input_code: sample code or workflow to analyze
  - available_profiles: list of 100+ available profiles
  - agent_type: detected agent type (optional, auto-detect if not specified)
Outputs:
  - selected_profile: best-matching profile from available_profiles
  - confidence_score: 0.0-1.0 confidence in selection
  - profile_differences: differences between selected and other top profiles
  - recommendation: whether to use selected profile or try alternative
```

### Profile Learning from Feedback
```
1. Profile initially selected based on agent type detection (95%+ accuracy)
2. Feedback collected from optimization results (quality, reduction percentages)
3. Profile parameters adjusted based on feedback (CMA-ES heuristic refinement)
4. Profile version incremented (minor: patch, major: significant changes)
5. Profile shared across DraCo instances (if sharing enabled)
6. A/B testing: compare current profile against new variant
7. If new profile shows >0.1% improvement: auto-update scheduled
```

## YAGNI-First Decision Ladder Enforcement (Phase 10 Component 3)

### Decision Ladder Levels (6 Levels)

| Level | Description | Token Reduction | Quality Impact | Enforcement |
|-------|-------------|-----------------|----------------|-------------|
| **L1** | Absolute minimum - only executable logic | 60-70% | 95%+ | Mandatory (phases 1-3) |
| **L2** | Essential logic + necessary imports | 70-80% | 93%+ | Mandatory (phases 1-4) |
| **L3** | Essential + frequently used utilities | 80-85% | 91%+ | Mandatory (all phases) |
| **L4** | Essential + commonly needed patterns | 85-88% | 90%+ | Developer approval (phases 5-6) |
| **L5** | Essential + language idioms | 88-90% | 89%+ | Developer consent (phases 7-8) |
| **L6** | Maximum inclusion (YAGNI relaxed) | 90%+ | 88%+ | Developer override only (phases 9-12) |

### YAGNI Enforcement Workflow
```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│               YAGNI-FIRST DECISION LADDER                    │
├─────────────────────┬─────────────────────┬───────────────┤
│   ASK: "Is this   │   IF YES:           │   IF NO:      │
│   absolutely      │     • Keep it       │     • Strip it│
│   needed?"        │     • Add to L1-L3  │     • Add to  │
│                   │     • Ladder L1-L3  │     • Ladder  │
│                   │     • Full retention│     • L4-L6   │
├─────────────────────┼─────────────────────┼───────────────┤
│   AUTOMATED CHECK: │• ML importance      │• Automatic    │
│   "Will this be  │   score > 0.3       │   stripping   │
│   used in production│• Historical usage   │   applied     │
│   code within 90  │• Developer intent   │   (Phase 5)   │
│   days?"          │• Usage patterns     │               │
└─────────────────────┴─────────────────────┴───────────────┘
```

### YAGNI Implementation per Agent

#### Claude Code YAGNI
- **Ladder Enforcement**: Strict L3 maximum without explicit approval
- **Skill Integration**: `.claude/skills/draco-yaml-filters.skill`
- **Auto-Approval**: 5-10% of L4-L6 items auto-approved based on usage history
- **Developer Override**: `// draco:keep` comment to override Ladder decision

#### Cursor YAGNI
- **Ladder Enforcement**: Flexible L4 maximum, L5 with prediction
- **Real-Time Feedback**: Immediate YAGNI decision display
- **Prediction Engine**: ML-based usage prediction for L5 items
- **Integration Point**: Sidebar YAGNI indicator

#### Copilot YAGNI
- **Ladder Enforcement**: L5 maximum, L6 with explicit consent
- **Suggestion Mode**: YAGNI recommendations as code suggestions
- **Commit Integration**: YAGNI decisions tracked in git commits
- **Dashboard**: YAGNI analytics dashboard

#### Codex YAGNI
- **Ladder Enforcement**: L3 maximum for auto, L5 with language model permission
- **Multi-Language**: Different ladder levels per language
- **Framework Awareness**: React vs. Django vs. different ladder settings
- **CLI Integration**: `draco yagni --decision-ladder level`

## Seamless Integration Without Workflow Disruption (Phase 10 Component 4)

### Integration Strategies (No Workflow Disruption)

#### 1. Drop-In Replacement
```
- DraCo replaces existing agent optimization automatically
- No code changes required
- Automatic agent detection
- Full backward compatibility
- Example: `draco optimize --project ./my-code` 
  optimizes without modifying any code or config
```

#### 2. Parallel Operation
```
- DraCo runs alongside existing agent optimization
- Separate pipelines for each
- Unified metrics dashboard
- Automatic conflict resolution
- Example: DraCo optimizes while Cursor's native optimization continues
```

#### 3. Gradual Adoption
```
- DraCo introduces optimization incrementally
- Start with Phase 1, add phases over time
- Metrics comparison at each phase
- Rollback if issues at any phase
- Example: Team adopts DraCo one phase per month
```

#### 4. Agent-Specific Adapter
```
- Custom adapter for agent's API/workflow
- Integration at agent's hook points
- Output format matching agent expectations
- Example: Full DraCo integration with unique agent APIs
```

#### 5. Real-Time Feedback Loop
```
- Real-time optimization during agent workflow
- Suggestions as agent works
- Latency < 100ms
- Quality monitoring continuous
- Example: DraCo suggests optimizations as Claude Code writes
```

#### 5. Version Compatibility Management
```
- Compatibility matrix for 50+ agent versions
- Backward compatible to v1.0
- Forward compatible with newer versions
- 6-month deprecation notice
- Example: DraCo works across Claude Code versions 2.x, 3.x
```

## Agent Detection & Profile Selection (Phase 10 Component 5)

### Agent Type Detection
```
Function: detect_agent_type()
Inputs:
  - input_sample: code sample or query (minimum 5-10 tokens)
  - context: optional context about project/type
Outputs:
  - detected_agent: one of 50+ agent types
  - confidence: 0.0-1.0 (95%+ accuracy typical)
  - alternatives: top 3 alternative agent types
  - agent_version: detected version
  - recommended_phases: [1,2,3,4,5,10] (phase recommendations)
  - yonagi_ladder_level: 3 (recommended YAGNI level)
```

### Detection Features (100+ features)
| Feature Category | Example Features |
|-----------------|-----------------|
| Code Style Patterns | "snake_case" variables, "camelCase" functions |
| Comment Conventions | "# TODO:", "# FIXME:" patterns |
| Import Patterns | `import os`, `from datetime import datetime` |
| Framework Usage | `react`, `django`, `fastapi`, `express` usage |
| Variable Naming | Hungarian notation, type-prefixed variables |
| Class Definitions | `class MyClass:` style, inheritance patterns |
| Function Patterns | `def my_func():`, `function myFunc() {}` styles |
| Documentation Style | Docstring formats (`"""`, `'''`, `///`) |
| Error Handling | `try/except`, `try/catch`, `exception` patterns |
| Loop Structures | `for`, `while`, `foreach` styles |
| Conditional Patterns | `if/elif/else`, `switch/case`, ternary operators |

### Profile Selection Algorithm
```
1. Detect agent type from input sample (95%+ accuracy)
2. Retrieve agent profile from 100+ pre-configured profiles
3. If confidence > 80%: use selected profile
4. If confidence 50-80%: try top 3 profiles, select best
5. If confidence < 50%: fall back to generic adapter (70-85% reduction)
6. Apply YAGNI ladder level from profile
7. Load appropriate ML models per profile
8. Configure MCP routing per profile
9. Enable/disable phases per profile
```

## Conflict Resolution Across Agents (Phase 10 Component 6)

### Conflict Types (20+ Identified)
| Conflict Type | Description | Resolution |
|---------------|-------------|------------|
| priority_conflict | Two rules with same priority for same token | Higher weight wins; or both applied (exclude + include = keep) |
| threshold_conflict | Two rules with overlapping thresholds | Merge thresholds: use min(exclude_threshold, include_threshold) |
| action_conflict | Two rules with opposite actions (exclude + include) | Priority determines winner; lower priority excluded |
| weight_conflict | Two rules with different weights | Weighted average; higher weight influences more |
| frequency_conflict | Rules based on conflicting frequency metrics | Use most recent measurement; or combine: AND logic |
| importance_conflict | Rules based on conflicting importance scores | Use DistilBERT consensus; or weighted average |
| schema_conflict | Rules violating YAML schema | Schema validation; auto-fix or disable rule |
| agent_conflict | Rules for different agents applied to same workflow | Agent-specific profiles; agent detection first |
| temporal_conflict | Rules based on time-dependent metrics | Use current metrics; or temporal weighting |
| version_conflict | Rules for different codebase versions | Version-aware rules; or upgrade/downgrade recommendations |
| language_conflict | Rules for different programming languages | Language-detection first; or language-specific rule sets |
| overall_conflict | Any conflict type overall | `draco integrate --conflict-resolution --auto` automatic resolution |

### Automatic Conflict Resolution
```
Function: auto_resolve_conflicts()
Inputs:
  - conflicts: list of detected conflict types (20+ possible)
  - resolution_strategy: "auto", "priority", "weighted", "manual"
  - agent_profile: current agent's profile
Outputs:
  - resolved_rules: list of rules with conflicts resolved
  - resolution_method: how each conflict was resolved
  - confidence: 0.0-1.0 confidence in resolutions
  - fallback_applied: whether fallback profile was used
```

